The original GeoJSON files are bundled for offline use. Their file hashes and
source paths are recorded in racer/data/source/provenance.json.

The training layouts are simplified approximations based on these coordinates.
Roads are widened to 32 image pixels. Corners are smoothed and nearby stretches
are moved apart so cars have room to turn without merging separate roads.
The prepared layouts are in racer/data/circuit-layouts.json and can be rebuilt
offline with scripts/build_circuit_layouts.py. The generated PNG examples and
road masks use these adapted layouts. They are not surveyed circuit boundaries.

Car physics retain each source map's scale. Elevation and banking are omitted.
The simulation compresses travel time by a factor of three, so its lap times
are suitable for comparing networks and are not real Formula 1 times.
